  "result": "I implemented fixed-width line numbers in ripgrep:\n\n- **`src/printer.rs`**: Added a `max_line_number_width: Option<usize>` field/builder method to `Printer`, and updated `line_number()` to left-pad the line-number string with spaces to that width when set (without truncating wider numbers).\n- **`src/args.rs`**: Added a corresponding `max_line_number_width` field to `Args`, parsed from a new `fixed-width-line-numbers` CLI flag, and wired it into the printer builder.\n- **`src/app.rs`**: Registered the new `--fixed-width-line-numbers NUM` flag (numeric, validated like `--max-columns`) with help text.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo build` succeeds.\n- Manual check: `rg -n --fixed-width-line-numbers=5 needle file` produces `    2:needle` (padded to width 5).\n- `cargo test --test integration line_number` \u2014 all 5 related tests pass.\n- Full `cargo test --test integration` has 74 pre-existing failures identical before and after my change (confirmed via stash comparison), so they're unrelated to this fix.\n\nNothing was committed, per instructions. `Cargo.lock` shows as modified only because it was already dirty at session start (lockfile format regenerated by cargo) \u2014 I did not intentionally touch it.",
